<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Publish generates a web.config when the project has none, and two of its defaults are wrong for
    this application on shared hosting.

    hostingModel is outofprocess, not the in-process default. In-process runs the app inside w3wp,
    so a 32-bit application pool - common on shared plans - simply cannot load a 64-bit
    self-contained build, and the module fails before it can write an error page: an empty 503.
    Out of process launches the executable separately, so the pool's bitness stops mattering.

    startupTimeLimit is 120 seconds by default. Program.cs runs Database.MigrateAsync() before
    app.Run(), so a first start against an empty database has to create the whole schema over a
    shared SQL host before it can serve anything. Exceeding the limit makes the module kill the
    process and return an empty 503 - no error page, nothing in the browser to say why. The
    generous limit costs nothing on a normal start, when nothing has to be migrated.

    stdout logging and detailed errors were on while the deployment was being brought up: a startup
    failure happens before any of the application's own logging exists, so the stdout file was the
    only account of it. Both are off now that it is serving.

      * stdoutLogEnabled writes every line the process emits to a file that nothing rotates or
        prunes. Left on it grows until the hosting quota stops the site.

      * ASPNETCORE_DETAILEDERRORS puts exception messages and stack traces in the browser. That is
        a description of the application's internals handed to whoever provoked the error.

    Turn them back on together, temporarily, if a deployment stops starting - the deploy workflow's
    "Fetch the server startup log" step reads that file when the health check fails.

    processPath and arguments are injected by publish; they are not repeated here.
-->
<configuration>
  <location path="." inheritInChildApplications="false">
    <system.webServer>
      <handlers>
        <add name="aspNetCore" path="*" verb="*" modules="AspNetCoreModuleV2" resourceType="Unspecified" />
      </handlers>

      <aspNetCore stdoutLogEnabled="false"
                  stdoutLogFile=".\logs\stdout"
                  hostingModel="outofprocess"
                  startupTimeLimit="600"
                  requestTimeout="00:10:00">
        <environmentVariables>
          <environmentVariable name="ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT" value="Production" />
        </environmentVariables>
      </aspNetCore>
    </system.webServer>
  </location>
</configuration>
